Does it count as &quot;HP recovery&quot; for purposes of the card when Absolute Zero gets hit with cold damage, but that turns into healing points? &nbsp;Talk about tank potential, plus the ability for some really sneaky combos. &nbsp;Imagine this setup: &nbsp;Legacy is buffing all characters for +2 damage, AZ has both modules and Focused Apertures. &nbsp;Every turn, AZ can Thermal Shockwave,&nbsp; damaging three targets for 4 cold damage each, hitting &nbsp;himself for 14 fire (12 + 2 from Legacy), but does 17 cold damage to himself via Iso Tranducer (14 +2 from Legacy +1 from Focused Apertures.). &nbsp; Net result: &nbsp;12 damage to opponents, +3 HP to AZ. &nbsp;(Add a Cryo Chamber, and this increases to +4) 

&nbsp;

After a few turns of this, AZ will probably be at full health. &nbsp;Now, he can Thermal Shockwave, doing 4 damage to three opponents, hit himself for 14, then use the Iso Transducer to bounce 17 cold damage back to a villain. &nbsp;End result, 21 pts damage to one villain, 4 pts damage to two other targets, -14 HP to AZ. &nbsp;You can save this until the last turn, or if it&#39;s a long slog of a game, simply start the cycle of healing over again.

